+# Changes
+
+## Round 1 — closing the round-0 gaps
+
+All five gaps in GAPS.md are closed this round, in rank order. Nothing the
+critic confirmed as matching was touched: bar heights are still computed from
+the data against the gridline scale, months are still named and centred at
+12px in calendar order, the single accent `#2f6db5` and the neutral greys are
+unchanged, gridlines are still `#d9d9d9` with a `#444444` baseline at zero,
+and there is still no legend, frame, gradient or shadow.
+
+### Gap 1 (major) — peak month called out: closed
+
+One label, `142.3k`, centred over the October bar (x-centre 504.5) with its
+baseline 6px above the bar's top edge (bar top y=93, label y=87), 12px,
+semi-bold, `#222222` (the title tone). It is the same compact form as the tick
+labels. The month and value are computed from the data (`indexOf(max)`), not
+hard-coded, so the callout follows the data if it changes. There is exactly one
+value label on the chart.
+
+### Gap 2 (minor) — 20k scale steps: closed
+
+The nice-step routine now targets about eight rules instead of four, which on
+this data gives ticks every 20k from 0 to 160k: nine rules counting the
+baseline, each labelled `0`, `20k` ... `160k` at 11px. The top rule (160k,
+y=60.5) sits just above the tallest bar (y=93); the baseline stays darker.
+
+### Gap 3 (minor) — title hierarchy: closed
+
+Title is now `Monthly revenue, 2025` at 18px semi-bold `#222222`, top-left,
+aligned with the plot's left edge (x=64). Directly under it, a 12px muted-grey
+(`#777777`) subtitle `USD, thousands` names both the unit and the scale the
+ticks are in. `(USD)` no longer appears in the title. The top margin grew from
+56 to 60 to give the subtitle room above the 160k rule.
+
+### Gap 4 (minor) — bar gap about a third of a bar: closed
+
+Bars are 35px wide with a 12px gap (0.34 of a bar, pitch 47). The first bar
+starts at the plot's left edge (x=64) and the last ends at its right edge
+(x=616). Month labels are centred under each bar.
+
+### Gap 5 (minor) — explicit white background: closed
+
+A full-canvas `<rect fill="#ffffff">` is now the first element in the SVG.
+
+### Checks
+
+- No overlaps: the peak label (y 78-87) is clear of the 160k rule (60.5) and
+  the 140k rule (97.5); the subtitle (bottom y=47, starting x=64) is clear of
+  the 160k tick label (y 56-64, ending x=54).
+- Nothing within 24px of the canvas edge except the left tick labels, which
+  start around x=32.
+- `npm test` passes (2/2). `npm run capture` written to `captures/chart.svg`
+  (sha256 c36670939a4d) and `captures/CAPTURE.md`.
+
+Left on purpose: nothing. All ranked gaps were closed.
+
+## Round 0 — first pass against STYLE.md
+
+Rewrote `src/chart.mjs`. The starting chart was twelve black bars filling the
+whole 600x300 canvas with no title, no scale, no month names, white numerals
+painted inside the bars, and raw values drawn above each bar so the tallest
+bar's label sat on the top edge. Every item in STYLE.md was missing.
+
+What changed, and the brief line it answers:
+
+- **Title with unit** — `Monthly revenue, 2025 (USD)` at 16px, top-left,
+  aligned to the plot's left edge.
+- **Twelve named bars in order** — bars are 62% of each month's slot with the
+  month abbreviation centred beneath each one at 12px.
+- **Usable scale** — horizontal gridlines at 50k, 100k, 150k with compact
+  labels and a darker 1px baseline at zero, snapped to half-pixels.
+- **One accent, neutral greys** — bars `#2f6db5`; title `#222`, labels `#555`,
+  gridlines `#d9d9d9`, baseline `#444`. No legend, border, gradients or
+  effects.
+- **Margins and legibility** — 640x400 canvas with 56/24/44/64 margins.
+- **Exactness** — bar heights from the data; per-bar callouts removed.
+- Added `role="img"` and an `aria-label`; escaped text.
