+# Gaps — round 1 (capture sha256 c36670939a4d)
+
+Judged against the report's reference chart. Ranked most important first.
+No gap below is major; all six things that matter (hierarchy, usable scale,
+month names, one accent colour, spacing, exactness) are met in this revision.
+
+## 1. Month labels are one step too large for tick text — minor
+
+- Where: captures/chart.svg:1, every month `<text ... font-size="12" fill="#555555">` at y=376
+  (CAPTURE.md:23-34 lists them all at 12px).
+- Why it matters: month labels are axis ticks, and they now sit at the same
+  size as the unit line ("USD, thousands", 12px) while the y-axis ticks are
+  11px. Tick text on both axes should be the same size and a step below the
+  subtitle so the eye goes title, bars, scale.
+- Closing it: set the month labels to 11px, same as the y-axis tick labels.
+  Keep them centred under their bars at the same y.
+
+## 2. Peak callout is larger than the tick text it sits among — minor
+
+- Where: captures/chart.svg:1, `<text x="504.5" y="87" ... font-size="12" font-weight="600" ...>142.3k</text>`
+  (CAPTURE.md:35).
+- Why it matters: the callout should read as an annotation on the scale,
+  not as a second subtitle. At 12px semi-bold it matches the subtitle line's
+  size; at tick size it stays subordinate to the title.
+- Closing it: render the callout at 11px, keep the semi-bold weight and the
+  dark title colour, keep it centred over the October bar with the same
+  6px clearance above the bar top (bar top y=93, label baseline y=87 is fine).
+
+## Verified as satisfied (no action)
+
+- Title 18px/600 dark grey top-left, 12px muted unit line under it
+  (chart.svg:1, CAPTURE.md:12-13).
+- Gridlines every 20k, labelled `0`…`160k` in compact form, light grey
+  lines, darker baseline at zero, scale starts at zero, top gridline (160k)
+  is the first round step above the 142.3k peak (chart.svg:1, CAPTURE.md:14-22).
+- Months by name in calendar order, each centred at bar x + 17.5 (chart.svg:1).
+- One accent `#2f6db5`, greys for text/lines, white background, no legend,
+  frame, gradient or shadow (CAPTURE.md:6-7).
+- Bars 35px wide with 12px gaps (about a third), plot spans x 64–616 of 640,
+  callout spans roughly x 484–525 and clears Sep (top y=112) and Nov (top
+  y=118); no text overlaps or runs off the edge (chart.svg:1).
+- Values map to the scale: at 1.85 px per k, Oct 263px = 142.2k, called out
+  as `142.3k`; all twelve bars agree with the reference within integer-pixel
+  rounding (chart.svg:1).
+
+verdict: pass
